          "tz": -300
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Patrickbot",
          "email": "patrick-bot@mulberrytree.us",
          "date": "2026-10-30 16:03:50.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity-quota test_49a",
        "message": "LU-20869 tests: speed up sanity-quota test_49a\n\ntest_49a set and deleted quota for every ID with a serial\nloop of lfs setquota, checked each ID range twice with the\nsame arguments, and ended with formatall and setupall.\nThe delete loop already removes every ID that was set, so\nthe reformat only cost time: no later test depends on it,\nand test_87, the only other user of lfs quota -a, sets the\nIDs it reads.\n\nRun the setquota and delete loops 8 ways in parallel,\ncheck each range once, and drop the reformat.\n\nAlso use NOSYNC during deletion and fail the test if deleting\neither quota type fails.\n\nOn rocky9 with 1000 IDs the test took 150, 151 and\n156 s before and 50, 40 and 40 s after. In CI the median\nreview run spends 210 s of 367 s in formatall and setupall,\nand the mean is 457 s over 6630 runs per 30 days; at about\n250 s saved per run this is about 460 hours per 30 days.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial testlist=sanity-quota env=ONLY=49a\nAssisted-by: Codex:gpt-6.1-sol\nSigned-off-by: Patrick Farrell <patrick@thelustrecollective.com>\nChange-Id: I71419e448ca139241e4e95b0b6d43c77888ef0c2\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
